1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,740
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,240
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,010
(Episode 28)

4
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:09,480
Yes, this is
Assistant Manager Kang Ye Ri.

5
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,520
Yes, I'll be right up.

6
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,790
CEO Jeon is asking for me.
I'll get going first.

7
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:19,290
All right.

8
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,100
By the way,
do you know Kang Da Mi, too?

9
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,140
- How?
- What?

10
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:35,770
I just happened to meet her
through Se Na.

11
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:38,810
I need to hurry up
and find an assistant, too.

12
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,350
See?

13
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,250
I told you that you needed at least
one assistant in your office.

14
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:46,650
People are lining up
to learn from you.

15
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:48,390
The company will find one for you.

16
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,020
No, it's fine.

17
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:52,860
I'll find someone
to work by my side myself.

18
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,060
Get back to work, Do Yun.

19
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:57,100
Take care.

20
00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:00,230
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

21
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:15,110
I heard back from Summit Investment.

22
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,780
- Is it good news?
- It depends on how you look at it,

23
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:19,850
but it's not bad.

24
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,650
Congratulations, ma'am.

25
00:01:21,890 --> 00:01:23,490
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

26
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:26,420
They want to have a meeting
at our office,

27
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,460
and they said they'd like...

28
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:29,090
to look around
the company beforehand.

29
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:32,530
- The company?
- It's an important matter,

30
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:34,900
so I'd like you to arrange it,
Assistant Manager Kang.

31
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,570
- You can handle it, right?
- Yes, of course.

32
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:46,340
How are things with Do Yun?
Any progress?

33
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,650
I think we've gotten
quite a bit closer than before.

34
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:50,680
Quite a bit?

35
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:53,650
I feel like I've been backing you
as much as I can.

36
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:56,120
How much more do I need to help?

37
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:59,260
No, you've already helped me
so much.

38
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:03,360
- I'll try harder.
- Trying hard alone isn't enough.

39
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:08,830
I keep you by my side
because I like the way you work.

40
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:10,100
I appreciate your abilities.

41
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:14,370
Yes, I'll continue to work hard
so that you won't be disappointed...

42
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:17,010
By the way,
the HR Team Leader told me...

43
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:19,980
that Do Yun recommended someone.

44
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,010
It's someone you know as well.

45
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:24,920
- Someone I know? Who?
- You remember Manager Kang Da Mi...

46
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,750
from the department store showroom,
right?

47
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:29,150
It seems she quit
the department store.

48
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:32,020
Though I'm not sure
if it was because of that incident.

49
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,130
So...

50
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:36,960
That manager or whatever
quit the department store,

51
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,430
and our Do Yun
offered her a position...

52
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:42,070
managing the pop-up store?

53
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:45,740
Yes. If I had known earlier,
I'd have stopped him,

54
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,740
but I only heard about it
right before coming up.

55
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,480
Fortunately, it seems
she had some conscience...

56
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,710
because she turned it down.

57
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:53,510
Do you really think
it was out of conscience?

58
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:56,810
She was scared of being exposed,

59
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,480
or the position wasn't
as high as she wanted.

60
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,090
Pardon?

61
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:02,450
A conscience is only for people...

62
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:04,890
who have something,
Assistant Manager Kang.

63
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,560
It seems Team Leader Cha...

64
00:03:08,030 --> 00:03:10,800
offered less money
than she expected.

65
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:15,300
She acts all righteous,

66
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:18,700
but in the end, she's just a snob.

67
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:22,440
- Team Leader Cha is just too kind.
- He isn't kind.

68
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:24,840
He's just a terrible judge
of character.

69
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:27,910
Assistant Manager Kang,

70
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,750
if you hear anything else
about that woman from now on,

71
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:32,580
report it all to me.

72
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:35,590
Yes, CEO Jeon, I'll do that.

73
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:56,270
The pay and working conditions
were all great, though.

74
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:01,680
I think I can just
treat the stain...

75
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,780
I said I'm going to throw it away.

76
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:08,120
Don't you understand
what I'm saying?

77
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,290
Manager Kang.

78
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,490
Don't you care about tomorrow?

79
00:04:14,230 --> 00:04:16,830
How could I work at a company
where a person like that is CEO?

80
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:18,460
No way, I could never do it.

81
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:22,830
I made the right call
turning it down. Totally.

82
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,240
All right.

83
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:31,680
Did you look into the people
around Do Yun's mother?

84
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:35,350
Yes. Surprisingly,

85
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,950
her network was far cleaner
than expected.

86
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,790
Cleaner?

87
00:04:41,650 --> 00:04:42,650
Well...

88
00:04:43,290 --> 00:04:45,890
The fact that it's too clean
bothers me.

89
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:49,160
Usually, by our age,

90
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:52,260
there are old friends or strained ties,
as one would expect,

91
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:54,000
yet around CEO Jeon,

92
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:56,370
no such relationships
were found at all.

93
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:57,840
Almost unnervingly so.

94
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:01,810
So her past is a blank slate,
is that it?

95
00:05:02,270 --> 00:05:05,010
Yes, there were no traces
at all, Madam Chairwoman.

96
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:10,210
How is that possible?

97
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:13,520
She's a person.
Any human being would...

98
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,120
No.

99
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:21,060
There must be a stone
we haven't turned.

100
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,400
- You're home?
- Yes.

101
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:29,800
Where's Mother?

102
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:33,040
Dr. Ju is here,
and they're having tea in her room.

103
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,510
Dr. Ju is here?

104
00:05:35,610 --> 00:05:37,110
Was he scheduled to come today?

105
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,250
No one is without a past.

106
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:48,690
Even if it takes time, dig deeper.

107
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:50,350
Yes, Madam Chairwoman.

108
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:04,100
Was today your checkup with Mother?

109
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:07,310
She called for me,
so I stopped by briefly.

110
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:08,770
Excuse me, then.

111
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:22,490
Mother, it's me.

112
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:33,360
You said you were going out.
You're back early.

113
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:35,730
I just went out to buy a few books.

114
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:40,640
Why did you call Dr. Ju, though?
Are you feeling unwell somewhere?

115
00:06:40,810 --> 00:06:43,910
No, I just had some errands for him.

116
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:48,480
I didn't mean to eavesdrop, Mother,

117
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:54,390
but it sounded like you asked Dr. Ju
to dig into someone's past.

118
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,520
So?

119
00:06:56,920 --> 00:07:00,260
Why would you ask Dr. Ju
to do something like that?

120
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:03,900
If there's someone to look into,
you could just ask me.

121
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:08,870
It's not company business.
It's my personal matter.

122
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:12,500
That hurts my feelings even more.

123
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,910
I'm your son.

124
00:07:15,710 --> 00:07:18,010
You have a perfectly capable son,
so why ask Dr. Ju...

125
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:19,880
to run your personal errands?

126
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,510
Honestly, I don't understand it
at all.

127
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,380
What's going on?

128
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,750
Sometimes, being parent and child...

129
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:29,920
can make things
all the more uncomfortable.

130
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,920
Just pretend you don't know.

131
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:38,160
- Mother.
- I told you to stay out of it.

132
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:43,530
- Yes, Mother.
- Okay.

133
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:45,000
What's that?

134
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,240
This?

135
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:50,210
I saw someone selling them
on the way,

136
00:07:50,270 --> 00:07:52,540
- and I bought some thinking of you.
- Really?

137
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:55,480
When you were young,
you loved walnut cakes.

138
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,350
Though you couldn't afford
to buy them often.

139
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,420
Would you like one?

140
00:08:01,090 --> 00:08:02,890
I held them close to my chest
so they would stay warm for you.

141
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:04,190
They're still hot.

142
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:15,100
Jun Sung.

143
00:08:21,110 --> 00:08:22,840
Yes, Mother.

144
00:08:23,610 --> 00:08:28,980
- It's me, Jun Sung. Yes.
- Don't eat this all by yourself.

145
00:08:29,150 --> 00:08:32,850
Share some with In Sung, okay?

146
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,850
Your father passed away early,

147
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:40,460
so to In Sung, you're both
an older brother and a father.

148
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:46,130
So you have to protect
our little In Sung.

149
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,270
Poor thing.

150
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:53,540
My poor boy, growing up without
ever knowing his father's face.

151
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:00,850
All right.

152
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:06,050
All right. Your ginseng chicken soup
is served.

153
00:09:06,550 --> 00:09:09,090
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

154
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:13,960
That's strange.

155
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,560
What is, Mi Mi?

156
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:19,860
The reishi mushrooms Mi Seon brought
are completely gone.

157
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,800
I went in to brew some for Mother,
but when I looked,

158
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:24,100
I couldn't find them anywhere.

159
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,970
It's not like they grew legs
and walked off. Where could they go?

160
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,870
The kids couldn't have eaten them.

161
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:31,740
What are you all whispering about?

162
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:35,350
She says the reishi mushrooms
are gone, Mrs. Choi.

163
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:37,680
Is that so?

164
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:42,120
- They must be somewhere.
- It's baffling, Mother.

165
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:44,120
Did you see them?

166
00:09:44,190 --> 00:09:47,590
Mi Seon bought them for me to eat,
and you showed them to me,

167
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,130
so I only looked at them.

168
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:52,430
I haven't seen them since. Not once.

169
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,200
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

170
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:57,800
- Mom...
- What's all this?

171
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:02,240
You want to know what this is?

172
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:10,210
Ta-da.
Hyung Gu sent me 300 of these.

173
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,780
For starters, let's put them...

174
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:14,120
on all the tables
in your restaurant.

175
00:10:15,390 --> 00:10:17,920
What's this? An ashtray?

176
00:10:19,890 --> 00:10:21,660
Restaurants went
smoke-free ages ago.

177
00:10:21,730 --> 00:10:23,960
Why on earth would you
put these ashtrays out?

178
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:27,260
Seriously, it's not an ashtray.

179
00:10:28,430 --> 00:10:29,970
If it's not an ashtray,
it looks like...

180
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,800
a stand for holding phones, maybe?

181
00:10:34,410 --> 00:10:35,870
Spot on, Grandma.

182
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:38,780
Goodness, Grandma,
you have the sharpest eyes here.

183
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:40,910
Wait, Hyung Gu?

184
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,980
Isn't that the friend
you co-signed a loan for...

185
00:10:43,150 --> 00:10:44,480
who took off with your money?

186
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:47,550
He should be paying back
what he owes you.

187
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:49,150
Why would he send
a bunch of this junk?

188
00:10:50,050 --> 00:10:52,290
Well, Mom, the thing is...

189
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:57,430
- Hold on, I need to talk to you.
- Talk then.

190
00:10:57,730 --> 00:10:59,860
I mean in private.

191
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:01,900
- Just a second. Hurry.
- Goodness.

192
00:11:02,230 --> 00:11:03,870
- Just a second.
- Hey, stop it.

193
00:11:03,930 --> 00:11:05,100
It won't take long.

194
00:11:05,970 --> 00:11:08,170
What are we supposed
to do with 300 of these?

195
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:11,240
Sell them on the secondhand marketplace
or something?

196
00:11:16,910 --> 00:11:18,420
What is it now?

197
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:20,850
Can't you see
I'm running a business?

198
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,150
Say it right here.

199
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:25,090
Right here?

200
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:30,030
Fine.

201
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:32,930
Mom.

202
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:36,430
Just this one last time,

203
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:39,870
could you help me
with 50,000 dollars?

204
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,440
- What?
- Hyung Gu is fleeing the country,

205
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,610
and he reached out saying
he'd hand over...

206
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,810
his factory business to me
for just 50,000 dollars.

207
00:11:50,050 --> 00:11:51,650
He owes me money anyway.

208
00:11:51,950 --> 00:11:54,750
If he owes you,
he should pay you back,

209
00:11:54,820 --> 00:11:56,750
or give you the factory if he can't.

210
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:00,060
Why should you have to give him
more money to take over his factory?

211
00:12:01,230 --> 00:12:04,200
Mom. At 50,000 dollars,

212
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,360
it's practically free.

213
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:11,570
I'm really confident
I can make it work this time.

214
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,870
People can't live
without smartphones these days.

215
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:17,580
Phone stands have become
an absolute necessity.

216
00:12:18,610 --> 00:12:20,480
If I keep coming up
with new designs,

217
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,610
I can build a solid business
and get back on my feet.

218
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:27,020
Mom, please, just this once.

219
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:29,650
Do you think I'm your personal ATM?

220
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:31,790
Mom.

221
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:33,920
I don't have any money.

222
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:35,390
What do you mean
you don't have money?

223
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:37,860
This house, the restaurant,

224
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:39,930
and the commercial building
across the street...

225
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,570
- they're all yours, Mom.
- They're only under my name.

226
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:44,870
Don't you know Grandma got them all
and passed them down to me?

227
00:12:45,770 --> 00:12:49,510
Besides, I've already helped you
more than enough.

228
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:51,040
I can't do any more.

229
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:53,380
Then why did you help Dae Chi?

230
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:57,680
Is Dae Chi your only child?

231
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,220
Why do you only help him?

232
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:05,160
Who said that?
Did he tell you I gave him money?

233
00:13:05,190 --> 00:13:06,260
Oh, please.

234
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:08,790
Some things are obvious
without being said.

235
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,960
We haven't just shared a room
for a day or two.

236
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,500
He used to lose sleep
every night over his debts,

237
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,870
and now he's sleeping like a log.

238
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:18,400
What does that mean?

239
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:21,370
It means his money troubles
have been sorted out.

240
00:13:22,470 --> 00:13:24,110
Who else could've given him
that money?

241
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,640
Who else would it be if not you?

242
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,180
Am I wrong?

243
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,650
Think whatever you want.

244
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:34,750
I really didn't want
to bring this up.

245
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:36,220
Mom.

246
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,160
When you pass away,

247
00:13:41,190 --> 00:13:42,860
who do you think
will hold your memorial rites?

248
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:45,730
It won't be Dae Chi, it'll be me.

249
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,100
And?

250
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,600
I'm the eldest grandson
in this family,

251
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:51,540
your eldest son.

252
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:56,010
So all I'm asking is for you...

253
00:13:56,810 --> 00:13:59,140
to trust me and back me up
till the end.

254
00:13:59,410 --> 00:14:01,010
Don't hold any rites for me.

255
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:04,450
I haven't even had a single meal
cooked by any of you,

256
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,280
so do you think I'd expect one
when I'm dead?

257
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,990
You're threatening me
with memorial rites?

258
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,120
You ungrateful brat.

259
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,290
Mom. Mom, that's not what...

260
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,230
Did I go too far?

261
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:25,740
I really didn't mean it that way.

262
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:29,570
Why is it so loud?

263
00:14:30,170 --> 00:14:31,340
What happened, Gang Nam?

264
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,440
Did you fight with Mom?

265
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,480
Hey, Kkangda.

266
00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:38,720
Don't you think Mom
is being way too unfair?

267
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,220
What do you mean?

268
00:14:40,550 --> 00:14:43,290
How could she give money
only to Dae Chi?

269
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:46,590
While her eldest son
is left with nothing.

270
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:51,260
Mom gave Dae Chi money?

271
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:54,200
Of course she did.
You know how Mom is.

272
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:58,100
Ever since we were little,
didn't the brilliant second son...

273
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,500
always come first?

274
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:04,580
Just because he was crazily good
at studying.

275
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:07,010
Where are you going?

276
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:09,610
To pick up Su Ah.

277
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,790
Mom gave Dae Chi money?

278
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,260
Just how much? Where did she get it?

279
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,240
What are you drinking so happily?

280
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,480
It's brewed reishi mushroom tea.

281
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:44,280
Reishi mushroom?
That's really expensive.

282
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:45,650
Honey, where did you get this?

283
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,920
Where else could something
this rare come from?

284
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,820
Did your mother bring it?

285
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:53,820
Did she come into our house again?

286
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:57,490
She didn't come inside,
so don't get worked up.

287
00:15:57,830 --> 00:16:00,230
She practically just tossed it
by the door and left.

288
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:04,640
She's unbelievable.
She cut ties with her only son...

289
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:06,600
and kicked him out,

290
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:07,840
so why act like
a fairy godmother now,

291
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:09,570
bringing all this stuff over?

292
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:11,180
She should just give us money.

293
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:13,480
It's not about being
a fairy godmother.

294
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:16,210
That's simply how a mother feels.

295
00:16:16,410 --> 00:16:18,850
Things like that
can't be bought with money.

296
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:21,390
You're a mother yourself.

297
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:23,920
Is it really so hard for you
to understand how my mother feels?

298
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:26,820
Yes, I don't understand it at all.

299
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:29,260
If she keeps hanging around
like this,

300
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:31,200
what happens if she runs into Ye Ri
face-to-face?

301
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,600
What will we do then?

302
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:36,070
What else? If that day comes,

303
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:38,800
the younger one
should greet her politely.

304
00:16:39,370 --> 00:16:40,440
Seriously...

305
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,040
- Who should I greet?
- Goodness.

306
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:45,240
- Seriously...
- You...

307
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:48,150
- When did you get here?
- Hey, sweetie, you're home?

308
00:16:48,650 --> 00:16:49,910
Why are you home so early?

309
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,820
I asked who I'm supposed to greet.

310
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:54,280
Is there someone
I shouldn't run into?

311
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,450
- Well, that's...
- No, I mean...

312
00:16:57,650 --> 00:17:01,730
The landlady.
She has such a cranky personality.

313
00:17:02,090 --> 00:17:03,860
I was worried
it would be annoying for you...

314
00:17:03,930 --> 00:17:06,260
if you ran into her,
so I was just expressing my concern,

315
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:08,700
and your dad said you just need
to greet her politely.

316
00:17:08,970 --> 00:17:12,240
- Right, honey?
- Right, exactly.

317
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:16,810
Although she doesn't seem
all that cranky to me.

318
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:20,380
From what I've seen,
she seems like a warm person.

319
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:25,680
I'm skipping dinner.
I need to watch my weight.

320
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,520
Oh, okay.

321
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:33,620
At home or outside, it never ends.

322
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,130
Park Ji Young's lifespan
is shortening by the minute.

323
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:51,610
How did you find out that
the debtor was suspended, Se Na?

324
00:17:52,010 --> 00:17:54,340
He promised to give me
a repayment plan,

325
00:17:54,410 --> 00:17:55,480
but he kept ignoring my...

326
00:17:57,950 --> 00:18:00,950
He wouldn't answer my calls.
So I called his company.

327
00:18:01,550 --> 00:18:04,120
At first, they made excuses,
saying he was away from his desk,

328
00:18:04,190 --> 00:18:07,420
but then a young guy told me,
"Manager Kang has been suspended,"

329
00:18:07,490 --> 00:18:09,490
"so he doesn't come
to work these days."

330
00:18:10,530 --> 00:18:13,000
I should go to his house again.

331
00:18:13,330 --> 00:18:14,330
Sweetheart.

332
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:17,000
You know that
if you blindly track down debtors,

333
00:18:17,270 --> 00:18:19,540
you could be violating the law
on illegal debt collection, right?

334
00:18:19,670 --> 00:18:22,770
I already received training
from our company manager, Dad.

335
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,510
I've been so busy lately.

336
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:28,710
I need to find a way to do this
without breaking the law.

337
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,720
- We're home.
- We're home.

338
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:36,890
- Oh, hey.
- Since you work at the same firm,

339
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:39,290
it's so nice to see
the two of you coming home together.

340
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:40,520
Welcome home.

341
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:43,460
He wanted to stay late to work
and told me to go ahead,

342
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:44,660
so I dragged him home myself.

343
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,570
- Have a seat, Seung Yun.
- What?

344
00:18:51,370 --> 00:18:52,400
All right.

345
00:18:54,510 --> 00:18:58,380
Good job. Take it easy, Seung Yun.

346
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:01,610
Get a feel for the office culture
and get to know people.

347
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:03,380
It'll be different from the US.

348
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:06,980
Yes, your uncle is right.

349
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:10,320
Since you worked only in the US
before becoming head designer,

350
00:19:10,590 --> 00:19:13,890
some executives are a bit concerned.

351
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:17,030
A designer just needs
to make good clothes.

352
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:18,860
Would I need any other skills?

353
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:23,300
Still, I'll definitely
take your advice to heart.

354
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:28,140
- Where's Grandma?
- She took an early nap,

355
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:30,170
so we were just
having tea ourselves.

356
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,180
Oh, right.

357
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,080
Do Yun, did you offer...

358
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:37,510
Manager Kang Da Mi a job
at the pop-up exhibition store,

359
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:39,120
only to get turned down?

360
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:42,350
Did Assistant Manager Kang
report that to you?

361
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:45,060
Does she report things like that
to you too, Mom?

362
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,620
That's not the point, son.

363
00:19:48,090 --> 00:19:51,860
Didn't I tell you not to bring
just anyone into your life?

364
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,300
Did you already forget that advice?

365
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,400
Wait.

366
00:19:56,470 --> 00:19:58,070
Manager Kang works
at the department store.

367
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,640
Did you ask her to switch over
to Hwanggeum Apparel, Do Yun?

368
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:05,080
- She quit.
- What? Why so suddenly?

369
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:06,580
I wonder.

370
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:09,380
Why did she quit?

371
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,680
I'm curious too.

372
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:15,390
Son,

373
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:17,750
why are you looking at me like that?

374
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,290
As Team Leader of Product Planning,

375
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:23,030
I just offered a job
to someone talented, Mom.

376
00:20:23,930 --> 00:20:25,900
I'm tired. I'll head upstairs first.

377
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:31,570
I'll excuse myself as well.

378
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,940
What's wrong with Do Yun?

379
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:42,710
He looked pretty upset with you.

380
00:20:43,350 --> 00:20:45,180
He seems to think
Manager Kang left...

381
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:47,720
the department store because of me.

382
00:20:48,190 --> 00:20:50,150
I don't understand why he cares
so much about...

383
00:20:50,150 --> 00:20:51,760
a mere department store employee.

384
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:56,090
Our Do Yun
is far too softhearted, darling.

385
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:03,130
(Balance: 2,643 Dollars)

386
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:08,010
I need to pay 600 dollars
for living expenses right away...

387
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:12,310
Plus this month's
credit card and phone bills...

388
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:15,710
Kang Da Mi, you're really hopeless.

389
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:19,780
What made you break
into your savings account...

390
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:21,550
and hand it over to Kang Dae Chi?

391
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:24,220
You should have just kept your job.

392
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:26,390
Who do you think you are, a hero?

393
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:33,600
Why did she come
all the way to my place...

394
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:35,830
Seriously.

395
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:41,410
Da Mi.

396
00:21:42,270 --> 00:21:44,740
You must be tired, Min Hee.
Why did you come?

397
00:21:44,810 --> 00:21:46,810
I was going to visit you later.

398
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:49,610
I'm so sorry.
It's really because of me...

399
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,050
Don't cry.

400
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:58,960
Who's the new showroom manager?
Are they nice to you?

401
00:21:59,990 --> 00:22:01,020
Yes.

402
00:22:01,290 --> 00:22:04,390
But every customer who visits
only asks for you.

403
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:06,000
They keep asking
where Manager Kang went.

404
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:07,960
Really?

405
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:10,730
You should have made up an excuse...

406
00:22:10,730 --> 00:22:12,900
and said I got scouted
by a great company.

407
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:15,710
Should I really say that?

408
00:22:24,050 --> 00:22:26,550
He refuses to eat dinner
just because I won't give him money?

409
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:30,490
He's turning 40,
and he still acts like a child.

410
00:22:31,190 --> 00:22:34,120
Fine, starve then.
It saves rice anyway.

411
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:39,730
Who's visiting now?

412
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:46,440
Manager Kang, what are you
planning to do now?

413
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:49,840
Me? Nothing at all.

414
00:22:51,170 --> 00:22:53,240
I've worked non-stop
since graduating college.

415
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,650
For a while, I'll sleep in...

416
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,480
and just lounge around,
eating and relaxing.

417
00:22:58,120 --> 00:22:59,880
Can you really afford to do that?

418
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:05,520
Of course. I have Mom.
Mom runs a business, after all.

419
00:23:05,690 --> 00:23:08,660
Why do you think I don't move out
and stay at Mom's place instead?

420
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:10,360
Because it doesn't cost a dime.

421
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:28,580
What is it, Mom?
Why are you looking at me like that?

422
00:23:29,050 --> 00:23:30,280
You'll do nothing...

423
00:23:30,350 --> 00:23:31,980
and just lounge around
eating and relaxing?

424
00:23:33,350 --> 00:23:36,550
Is that your plan after quitting your job
without discussing it?

425
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:39,090
Why are you eavesdropping
on my conversation?

426
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:41,290
I told you I'd take care
of my own business.

427
00:23:41,290 --> 00:23:42,690
I said don't worry about it.

428
00:23:42,930 --> 00:23:45,030
How can I not worry?
I'm your mother.

429
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:47,330
What were you thinking,

430
00:23:47,930 --> 00:23:50,130
and what on earth happened
that made you quit...

431
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,900
a perfectly good job
with a steady paycheck?

432
00:23:52,470 --> 00:23:53,840
Wouldn't you be curious
if you were me?

433
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:56,410
Wouldn't you be worried?

434
00:23:57,110 --> 00:23:59,940
I had to make a decision quickly
without time to consult anyone,

435
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,280
and since I already quit,

436
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:04,050
I really don't want
to talk about it, Mom.

437
00:24:04,710 --> 00:24:07,320
The reason I told my junior earlier
about lounging around and eating...

438
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:10,950
Never mind.

439
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:15,290
All three of my grown children...

440
00:24:15,460 --> 00:24:18,330
are cooped up in this house,
and none of you care...

441
00:24:18,760 --> 00:24:20,160
how miserable that makes me feel.

442
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:35,510
(Statement of Facts
and Circumstances)

443
00:24:35,710 --> 00:24:38,380
That jerk Kim Pro
told me to invest, so I did.

444
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:41,280
What's wrong with
investing my own money?

445
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:44,390
(I met Deputy Manager Kim Dong Seok
through work...)

446
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:46,160
(and received a personal
investment proposal from him.)

447
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:51,390
Seriously, if you take text messages
out of context,

448
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:53,700
everything looks suspicious.

449
00:24:57,830 --> 00:25:00,840
- What?
- Ever heard of knocking?

450
00:25:01,710 --> 00:25:02,710
You startled me.

451
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:05,710
What's wrong with you?
Is this room yours alone?

452
00:25:06,910 --> 00:25:08,410
What are you looking at
that made you react so late?

453
00:25:10,350 --> 00:25:12,920
Hey, are you looking at
that kind of stuff in the morning?

454
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:14,920
Stop talking nonsense.

455
00:25:15,190 --> 00:25:16,290
Do you think I'm like you?

456
00:25:17,650 --> 00:25:19,660
Aren't you going to work?
Why are you lying around like this?

457
00:25:19,860 --> 00:25:21,120
I'm working from home.

458
00:25:21,490 --> 00:25:22,590
From home?

459
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:24,230
Give me a break.

460
00:25:24,430 --> 00:25:26,530
You acted like
your job was so important,

461
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:29,200
making a huge fuss
that the company would collapse...

462
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,330
if you didn't show up.

463
00:25:37,770 --> 00:25:39,640
- Dad!
- Goodness.

464
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:42,280
You startled me, Su Ah.

465
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:44,180
When you enter
someone else's room...

466
00:25:44,250 --> 00:25:46,280
It's Dad's room,
so how is it someone else's?

467
00:25:46,620 --> 00:25:47,620
Exactly.

468
00:25:48,450 --> 00:25:50,820
Are you all ready?
We're going to be late.

469
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:54,860
Hey, working from home or not,
fix your posture.

470
00:25:55,630 --> 00:25:58,830
Sit up straight while working.
Are you a child?

471
00:25:59,230 --> 00:26:02,000
Let's go.
Your uncle is just a big baby.

472
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:05,840
Unbelievable.

473
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:11,940
What now? What is it this time?

474
00:26:12,980 --> 00:26:15,850
Kang Dae Chi, by any chance,
did you take money from Mom too?

475
00:26:16,210 --> 00:26:17,210
Why do you ask?

476
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:21,120
Did you take it or not?
Just answer me, hurry.

477
00:26:21,620 --> 00:26:23,090
Why are you asking me that?

478
00:26:23,890 --> 00:26:24,890
If you're curious,

479
00:26:25,590 --> 00:26:27,360
go ask Mom yourself.

480
00:26:29,060 --> 00:26:31,730
Is that so?
You can't tell me yourself?

481
00:26:33,060 --> 00:26:34,230
I'm busy.

482
00:26:34,830 --> 00:26:36,470
I'm doing some very important work.

483
00:26:37,270 --> 00:26:38,300
Could you please get out?

484
00:26:55,650 --> 00:26:57,650
(Regular Payment 200 Dollars,
Total 80,000 Dollars)

485
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:01,020
Before Da Mi gets married,

486
00:27:01,690 --> 00:27:04,330
I need to deposit this money
back quickly.

487
00:27:06,130 --> 00:27:07,760
- Mom.
- Goodness! You scared me.

488
00:27:09,330 --> 00:27:11,070
- Hey...
- What's this?

489
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:13,800
It's nothing. Give it here.

490
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:16,970
What is it that you were staring at
so intensely?

491
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:19,810
I told you to give it back, okay?

492
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:27,820
Hello?

493
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:28,890
I'm sorry for calling so early.

494
00:27:28,950 --> 00:27:30,250
Could we possibly meet for a moment?

495
00:27:30,590 --> 00:27:32,620
Meet me? Why again...

496
00:27:32,620 --> 00:27:33,890
I have something to tell you
in person.

497
00:27:35,030 --> 00:27:36,160
I'm in front of the restaurant
right now.

498
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:37,460
If you don't have any other plans,

499
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:38,960
let's meet in an hour
in front of the restaurant.

500
00:27:42,170 --> 00:27:44,700
All right, I understand. Okay.

501
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:51,840
Who was that?

502
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:54,510
Just a guy I know.

503
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,130
(Mission: Mompossible)

504
00:28:16,230 --> 00:28:20,040
I don't even need to look to know
whose pocket that money ended up in.

505
00:28:20,100 --> 00:28:22,640
And Da Mi found out about it.

506
00:28:22,770 --> 00:28:24,710
How did Da Mi find out?

507
00:28:25,110 --> 00:28:27,980
Kang Da Mi, isn't it your dream
to become a fashion designer?

508
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:30,050
A personal assistant?

509
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:33,720
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
